---
description: Extract Tailwind to a CSS module class when a tag has more than two utilities
globs: apps/web/**/*.{tsx,jsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Web class names

If an HTML tag would have more than two Tailwind utilities, do not put them in `className`. Add a class in the nearest `*.module.css` and use that.

Two utilities or fewer may stay on the tag.

```tsx
// BAD
<main className="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-2xl flex-1 flex-col gap-6 px-6 py-24">

// GOOD
<main className={styles.main}>
```

In the CSS module, pull tokens from the UI stylesheet and `@apply` the utilities.

```css
@reference '@repo/ui/globals.css';

.main {
  @apply mx-auto flex w-full max-w-2xl flex-1 flex-col gap-6 px-6 py-24;
}
```

Do not use `style={{}}` for layout when a class would do.
